WEBVTT

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:02.668
I know you. Oliver Trask.

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:04.044
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:04.253 --> 00:00:07.004
Next time you wanna be alone
with my girlfriend, I can stay home.

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:10.673
Everybody who knows me
for more than five minutes hates my guts.

00:00:10.882 --> 00:00:12.800
- I'm so stupid!
- Take it easy.

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:16.052
So in theory, Julie Cooper
could become your stepmother.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.553
Don't even say it.

00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:19.512
I can start over, have a new life.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:22.723
I never really wanted to be
a financial planner. Or a thief.

00:00:22.931 --> 00:00:25.224
I think Jimmy and I might've
gone into business together.

00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:28.685
- You are drunk.
- You guys are like brother and sister.

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:30.186
You guys could be related.

00:00:30.394 --> 00:00:32.729
- What's wrong?
- I just took a whole bunch of pills.

00:00:32.937 --> 00:00:35.814
- We're leaving. See you soon.
- What if he didn't try to kill himself?

00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:38.149
- What?
- He wouldn't go to the hospital.

00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:40.025
I can't leave him alone tonight.

00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:42.402
Just go home,
and I'll see you in the morning.

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:46.237
You did accuse the guy
of faking a suicide attempt.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.822
- No, I didn't. I just didn't believe him.
- Oh, okay.

00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:51.324
Hard to believe such blind compassion
upset Marissa.

00:00:51.532 --> 00:00:52.700
You should work for UNICEF.

00:00:52.908 --> 00:00:55.243
I don't trust him.
Something about Oliver is off.

00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:57.661
Yeah. He tried to kill himself.

00:00:57.953 --> 00:01:00.538
Or he faked it, man.
Either way, it's pretty off.

00:01:00.746 --> 00:01:03.581
Every day it seems Marissa and I
are fighting about this guy.

00:01:03.748 --> 00:01:05.708
- I don't even know why.
- Ryan, I'm no girl...

00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:09.669
Although I did spend several summers
at Camp Takaho being called such.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:13.588
- Maybe your jealousy's getting in the way.
- Yeah, except I'm not jealous.

00:01:13.796 --> 00:01:15.464
Jealous? Why would I be jealous?

00:01:15.672 --> 00:01:19.300
Because Oliver is insanely wealthy
and well-traveled. He's a Dapper Don.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.301
- And I'm not.
- But on the other hand...

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:24.886
...he's also clinically depressed
and chemically dependent. So you know...

00:01:25.095 --> 00:01:27.096
...it all comes out in the wash, really.

00:01:27.805 --> 00:01:30.098
You want my advice?
Just embrace the friend, man.

00:01:30.306 --> 00:01:33.142
- You should make peace with this guy.
- Maybe you're right.

00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:36.894
Or, I don't know, you could enjoy
the arguing with Marissa.

00:01:37.269 --> 00:01:39.395
Sparks flying. Her yin to your yang.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:43.064
Could be nice for your relationship.
I'd imagine.

00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:45.816
- Why, you and Anna don't fight?
- We're all yang, Ryan.

00:01:46.025 --> 00:01:49.485
What would we fight about? We like
the same things, have the same interests.

00:01:49.694 --> 00:01:51.695
- It's ridiculous.
- That sounds terrible.

00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:54.196
- We're sharing the same brain.
- Not me and Marissa.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:58.241
Let me ask you something. Am I dating
the female me? Like me, but as a girl?

00:01:58.449 --> 00:02:00.075
I don't know. That's disgusting.

00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:01.993
True.

00:02:02.535 --> 00:02:04.828
- I gotta go.
- Catch you later, Marissa.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.081
- Go what?
- Gotta go embrace the friend.

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:16.335
Hi. Hey.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.379
- How are you?
- I'm okay.

00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:21.839
- How's Oliver?
- You really want to know?

00:02:22.297 --> 00:02:23.840
Yeah. Yeah, I do.

00:02:24.048 --> 00:02:27.092
He feels bad. He doesn't understand
why he took a bunch of pills...

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.761
...and you and I got in a fight over it.
By the way, I don't get it, either.

00:02:30.969 --> 00:02:32.429
Right. I know.

00:02:32.887 --> 00:02:35.931
And I know I've been
a little weird about everything.

00:02:36.181 --> 00:02:39.016
But he's your friend. So he's my friend.

00:02:40.809 --> 00:02:45.478
I know. I'm not saying I might not
get weird about it again...

00:02:45.979 --> 00:02:47.271
...but I wanna try.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.981
You wanna hang out with him,
you want me to, it's okay.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.442
It's better than okay. It's... It's great.

00:02:53.942 --> 00:02:55.526
- Great?
- Yeah, well...

00:02:55.735 --> 00:02:58.487
"Great" is probably pushing it a little.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.572
- But definitely good.
- Thanks.

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:07.659
Ryan. Marissa. I want you to meet
our new transfer student.

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:09.619
He says you're all friends.

00:03:56.148 --> 00:03:57.649
Hey. So I was thinking...

00:03:57.857 --> 00:04:01.151
...maybe after school we could
go play a little bit of Jenga. Yeah?

00:04:01.484 --> 00:04:02.985
No.

00:04:03.194 --> 00:04:06.988
Or we could go get some comics.
We haven't done that in a while.

00:04:07.988 --> 00:04:10.865
Okay. We could go to South Coast Plaza
and quietly mock people.

00:04:11.074 --> 00:04:13.575
Or why don't we try
and do something different?

00:04:13.784 --> 00:04:16.452
Like... Check it out. I got some ideas.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.453
- Muscle-car racing.
- What?

00:04:18.662 --> 00:04:22.539
Or we could learn Israeli self-defense.
They call it Krav Maga.

00:04:22.748 --> 00:04:24.332
- Seth. Come on.
- Krav Maga.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.667
- What?
- Why don't we go to the IMAX theatre...

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:30.461
...and see the movie on migrating birds?
- IMAX, Anna? We're cooler than that.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:34.005
I think we're past that. Why don't we
take Luke's Sea-Doo out for a spin?

00:04:34.213 --> 00:04:36.756
I'm looking to
branch out into different water sports.

00:04:36.965 --> 00:04:39.925
- Okay. I'll support that.
- Good. If not, we can argue about it.

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:42.969
No, I think it's good.
It's important that we change things up.

00:04:43.177 --> 00:04:45.970
- We don't want to get boring.
- Good. I think it's important...

00:04:46.179 --> 00:04:50.598
...for us to not always do the same stuff
or dress the same, or whatever.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.809
- Damn it.
- Wow.

00:04:54.476 --> 00:04:57.269
You take Israeli self-defense.
I'll take muscle cars.

00:04:57.519 --> 00:04:59.479
- Got yourself a little deal there.
- Partner.

00:05:01.939 --> 00:05:04.732
- Hey.
- Hey. Oliver, what's up, man?

00:05:04.941 --> 00:05:07.400
- You visiting Harbor?
- Actually, Oliver goes here now.

00:05:07.609 --> 00:05:08.985
Never too late for a new start.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.944
What a surprise.

00:05:11.361 --> 00:05:13.571
- You didn't tell anyone?
- I didn't think you meant it.

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.865
Of course. I have more friends here
than I did at my last school.

00:05:17.073 --> 00:05:19.658
Anyways, I'm gonna go wash up.
It's tuna-melt Monday.

00:05:19.867 --> 00:05:21.493
- And we love tuna melts.
- Yes, we do.

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:23.285
I was looking forward, though...

00:05:23.494 --> 00:05:25.995
...to sampling some of the other items
on the menu.

00:05:27.038 --> 00:05:30.790
- Good. That's good. That's great.
- Bye-bye.

00:05:31.832 --> 00:05:35.710
I was gonna take Oliver to the bookstore,
since we both have free periods now.

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:38.587
Marissa and I have, like,
the exact same schedule.

00:05:38.795 --> 00:05:40.046
- What are the odds?
- Crazy.

00:05:41.422 --> 00:05:42.714
Have fun.

00:05:42.923 --> 00:05:44.132
Okay. Come on.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.716
Later on.

00:05:46.967 --> 00:05:50.427
There it is, man. Tuna melts, Ryan.
What am I gonna have to give up next?

00:05:50.636 --> 00:05:51.720
Oliver goes here.

00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:54.513
I was trying to talk about myself,
but I did notice.

00:05:54.722 --> 00:05:58.015
- You don't find that completely...?
- Embrace the friend, okay?

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:02.518
- I'm sure there's a good explanation.
- Seth. Come on.

00:06:03.269 --> 00:06:04.853
I gotta go.

00:06:06.771 --> 00:06:10.898
And my 12:00? Right.
The 16-year-old with his third DUI.

00:06:11.107 --> 00:06:14.567
What do I have at 6?
The travel agent who falsely advertised...

00:06:14.776 --> 00:06:18.820
...the Bahamian beach house. What a day.
All right. Thanks, Cory. Bye.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.488
Four years at Berkeley Law,
15 as a public defender...

00:06:21.697 --> 00:06:25.991
...so I could become Judge Judy.
- I like her. She's tough, but fair.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.868
I watch a lot of daytime TV.
What's going on?

00:06:29.077 --> 00:06:32.704
- Tomorrow, we're going to lunch.
- You couldn't have told me on the phone?

00:06:32.954 --> 00:06:34.038
At the Lighthouse.

00:06:34.246 --> 00:06:36.164
Yeah, except for
the Lighthouse is closed.

00:06:36.373 --> 00:06:38.541
- Forever.
- Well, I got them to open it up again.

00:06:38.749 --> 00:06:40.876
So we could take a look,
make sure we wanna buy it.

00:06:41.084 --> 00:06:43.794
- Are you serious?
- I sure am. You can thank me later.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:48.380
We were five martinis deep, we were
joking. There was singing involved.

00:06:48.589 --> 00:06:50.673
I remember.
You alienated several waitresses.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.008
- Well, that one liked me.
- You were drunk.

00:06:53.217 --> 00:06:55.885
That's my point.
We cannot open a restaurant.

00:06:56.052 --> 00:06:58.512
- That's crazy.
- Why? Why is that so crazy?

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.555
We don't know anything
about running one.

00:07:00.763 --> 00:07:02.723
You managed the Lighthouse
for two years.

00:07:02.931 --> 00:07:04.223
Two summers.

00:07:04.432 --> 00:07:07.851
And I was stoned and drunk, in college.
It was the '80s.

00:07:08.059 --> 00:07:10.060
You might wanna keep that
from the investors.

00:07:10.269 --> 00:07:13.146
- Restaurants fail.
- Not all of them.

00:07:13.354 --> 00:07:15.481
- I don't have the capital.
- I'm working on that.

00:07:15.689 --> 00:07:19.733
- Look, it's not a good time for me.
- That's exactly my point.

00:07:19.942 --> 00:07:22.985
If you don't find something soon,
the next stop for you is Phoenix.

00:07:23.194 --> 00:07:25.570
The way I look at it,
you got nothing to lose.

00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:27.405
And we both have everything to gain.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.782
So, come on.
Am I gonna see you tomorrow?

00:07:32.241 --> 00:07:35.660
- I'm sorry. I can't do lunch today.
- But what about tomorrow?

00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:37.286
It's a little hectic right now.

00:07:37.494 --> 00:07:40.830
The Fred Segal sale is happening.
I was thinking maybe Nobu. A road trip.

00:07:41.038 --> 00:07:42.706
That's even less likely than lunch.

00:07:42.914 --> 00:07:44.248
- Movie?
- No.

00:07:44.499 --> 00:07:45.958
Coffee?

00:07:47.626 --> 00:07:50.753
Julie, I really appreciate your desire
to be such good friends...

00:07:50.961 --> 00:07:54.547
...but the thing about good friends
is that when they want something...

00:07:54.755 --> 00:07:56.298
...they just ask.

00:07:57.423 --> 00:08:00.092
The interior design job.
I know it's available. I want it.

00:08:03.802 --> 00:08:07.138
I thought you wanted me
to water your plants or babysit Kaitlin.

00:08:07.346 --> 00:08:10.765
Because you don't take me seriously
as a working woman, as a designer.

00:08:10.974 --> 00:08:13.267
You're not really experienced, qualified.

00:08:13.475 --> 00:08:15.351
Before I had Marissa,
I did lots of design work.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.936
You had Marissa when you were 18.

00:08:18.228 --> 00:08:20.896
I know your usual home designer
fell out at the last minute.

00:08:21.063 --> 00:08:22.689
I know you have no one.

00:08:22.981 --> 00:08:24.607
Caleb. Pillow talk.

00:08:24.816 --> 00:08:28.234
- He thought the idea was inspired.
- Well, it's thinking outside the box.

00:08:28.443 --> 00:08:31.862
He told me he's staying out of it, though.
That it's up to you.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.865
Look. One house, one shot. If I screw up,
you can fire me yourself. It's a win-win.

00:08:43.661 --> 00:08:45.495
Hi.

00:08:45.704 --> 00:08:48.997
- What's so funny?
- Danny. He's, like, the funniest guy ever.

00:08:49.206 --> 00:08:52.374
Yeah? Hey, man. I'm Seth.
Good to meet you.

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:56.919
Your yellowtail is not as fresh as mine.
Dare to taste my albacore?

00:09:02.422 --> 00:09:04.590
He's, like, straight out
of a Bruce Lee movie.

00:09:08.843 --> 00:09:11.887
Hey, who took the jelly
out of your doughnut?

00:09:12.095 --> 00:09:14.513
Somebody call CSI,
we got ourselves a cold one here.

00:09:15.972 --> 00:09:18.474
- CSI!
- Hey, tag that toe.

00:09:21.601 --> 00:09:26.020
All right, well, somebody call ER.
I think Luke's gonna bust a gut.

00:09:31.691 --> 00:09:34.276
- I don't get it.
- Hey. Looks like we both got tuna.

00:09:34.526 --> 00:09:37.736
Mine's just raw and missing cheese.

00:09:43.531 --> 00:09:45.908
Time for class.
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.951
Hey, don't fall in.

00:10:07.213 --> 00:10:08.422
Hey.

00:10:09.214 --> 00:10:10.423
Is this seat available?

00:10:11.799 --> 00:10:14.718
- Sure. Yeah.
- Wow.

00:10:15.968 --> 00:10:18.678
- I'm so behind already.
- I know the feeling.

00:10:19.054 --> 00:10:21.472
Does junior year ever get easier?

00:10:22.681 --> 00:10:23.973
I thought you were a senior.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.684
Not a good one. And Harbor,
being as competitive as it is...

00:10:27.892 --> 00:10:30.060
...not all my credits transferred.

00:10:30.394 --> 00:10:33.229
- But you still wanted to come here?
- Wasn't up to me.

00:10:33.438 --> 00:10:37.148
My parents insisted.
Put the paperwork in a while ago.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.359
Why transfer at all,
a little over a semester from graduating?

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:44.820
It just wasn't working for me at Pacific.

00:10:45.445 --> 00:10:46.863
Because?

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:51.907
Because there was an incident.

00:10:55.243 --> 00:10:56.702
What kind of incident?

00:11:01.372 --> 00:11:03.248
Look, I've made some mistakes in my life.

00:11:03.456 --> 00:11:05.875
I don't think that's a surprise.
Or a secret.

00:11:06.083 --> 00:11:09.585
But if you could just
give me a chance, Ryan.

00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:12.712
Just let me in,
like I know people let you in.

00:11:13.463 --> 00:11:17.674
I could finally start over.
That's really all I want.

00:11:20.467 --> 00:11:22.218
- Hey, guys.
- Hi.

00:11:22.427 --> 00:11:23.636
Hey.

00:11:23.844 --> 00:11:26.262
I thought maybe we could
go to Oliver's after school.

00:11:26.471 --> 00:11:29.181
- Order in some room service.
- Yeah. You wanna come?

00:11:29.389 --> 00:11:32.058
- I was gonna help him with his French.
- French?

00:11:33.642 --> 00:11:37.269
- Didn't you live in Paris a couple years?
- A year. When I was 13.

00:11:37.478 --> 00:11:39.062
And you need Marissa to help you?

00:11:39.312 --> 00:11:41.105
Well, sweet-talking my way
into a club...

00:11:41.313 --> 00:11:44.399
...isn't the same
as conjugating the infinitive.

00:11:45.107 --> 00:11:48.568
Right. You guys go ahead.
I told Seth I'd meet him back home.

00:12:04.453 --> 00:12:08.080
- You sure you don't wanna come?
- Yeah. I trust you.

00:12:08.914 --> 00:12:10.582
You should.

00:12:19.712 --> 00:12:22.506
- I don't trust him.
- Trust who?

00:12:22.798 --> 00:12:25.466
Summer's new boyfriend or whatever.

00:12:25.633 --> 00:12:28.509
- Something sort of seems off about him.
- Off how?

00:12:28.718 --> 00:12:31.261
I don't know. He's just not funny.

00:12:31.636 --> 00:12:33.429
You know what I'm talking about.
He's big.

00:12:33.638 --> 00:12:36.556
But big isn't necessarily funny. It's cheap.

00:12:36.973 --> 00:12:38.683
He said there was an incident.

00:12:38.891 --> 00:12:42.185
- Big funny guy did?
- No. Oliver.

00:12:42.977 --> 00:12:45.645
Can we forget Oliver for five seconds
and talk about me?

00:12:45.812 --> 00:12:48.022
It's the reason he left Pacific.
What if he's violent?

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:49.689
New guy shows up. Violent. Angry.

00:12:49.898 --> 00:12:51.524
Prone to punching people.
That'd be weird.

00:12:51.732 --> 00:12:54.109
He needs help with his French?
He lived in France.

00:12:54.317 --> 00:12:57.403
We should call the cops.
Oliver lost his grasp on the subjunctive.

00:12:57.611 --> 00:12:59.279
Fajitas are served.

00:13:00.821 --> 00:13:04.532
Nothing adds up.
And if I try to say anything to Marissa...

00:13:05.533 --> 00:13:07.534
- Maybe there's somebody I can talk to.
- Yeah.

00:13:07.742 --> 00:13:11.620
Or you could break into the file room and
steal his bio. Or you can be a grownup...

00:13:11.828 --> 00:13:15.706
...forget about it and move on. Okay?
Like I am. To the fajitas.

00:13:39.345 --> 00:13:41.305
Hey, can I help you?

00:13:43.056 --> 00:13:44.891
I forgot a book in my locker.

00:13:49.852 --> 00:13:51.978
All right. It's open. Make it quick.

00:14:42.427 --> 00:14:44.011
Hey, what are you doing?

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.725
I don't think I need to explain
what a serious offense this is.

00:14:53.934 --> 00:14:57.186
We understand, and believe me
when I tell you, Ryan will be punished.

00:14:57.394 --> 00:14:58.728
I'm afraid it won't end there.

00:14:58.937 --> 00:15:01.647
This matter will be presented
to the disciplinary committee.

00:15:01.855 --> 00:15:05.024
Suspension, even expulsion,
are not out of the question.

00:15:05.232 --> 00:15:07.359
The school must do
what it deems appropriate.

00:15:07.567 --> 00:15:10.236
But understand that this
is very uncharacteristic of Ryan.

00:15:10.402 --> 00:15:15.155
Indeed. Mr. Atwood and Harbor
seem like a remarkably good fit.

00:15:15.364 --> 00:15:18.783
Which leads me to wonder,
why would you do this?

00:15:20.033 --> 00:15:25.453
I just... I don't trust this kid.
Oliver. He seems suspicious.

00:15:25.662 --> 00:15:27.663
- Suddenly he's going here now.
- I assure you...

00:15:27.872 --> 00:15:30.665
...Oliver went through the same
screening process as any student.

00:15:30.873 --> 00:15:33.292
He has a history of instability.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.876
I was concerned.

00:15:36.252 --> 00:15:38.378
- For Marissa.
- Has he made any threats to her?

00:15:38.587 --> 00:15:40.046
Anything to warrant your suspicions?

00:15:40.254 --> 00:15:42.798
No, but he's been spending
a lot of time with her.

00:15:43.798 --> 00:15:46.758
And there's this letter in his file...

00:15:46.967 --> 00:15:49.051
- A confidential letter.
- Says they found him...

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.637
...in the men's bathroom at Pacific,
having cut his wrists...

00:15:53.054 --> 00:15:54.888
...over a girl.

00:15:56.098 --> 00:15:58.516
She filed a restraining order.
That's why he left.

00:15:58.808 --> 00:16:00.517
- Is this true?
- Two years ago.

00:16:00.725 --> 00:16:02.852
Since then he's been institutionalized.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.979
And everyone involved
in Mr. Trask's rehabilitation...

00:16:06.187 --> 00:16:09.106
...believed his best chance
was a change in his environment.

00:16:09.314 --> 00:16:11.899
And the school was receptive to him
despite his history?

00:16:12.399 --> 00:16:16.235
Harbor is known to make exceptions
for students with troubled backgrounds...

00:16:16.485 --> 00:16:20.029
...but who show extraordinary promise.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:23.406
- I'm sorry.
- We are too.

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:26.533
We will see you at 3 p.m.
For detention...

00:16:26.742 --> 00:16:30.828
...which you will attend every day
until the committee reaches its verdict.

00:16:31.578 --> 00:16:33.329
Thank you, Dr. Kim.

00:16:34.038 --> 00:16:35.289
Thank you.

00:16:40.625 --> 00:16:42.627
- Seth. Hey.
- Hey.

00:16:42.835 --> 00:16:44.419
- I have a surprise for you.
- Really?

00:16:45.045 --> 00:16:46.754
Two tickets to see Bright Eyes.

00:16:46.963 --> 00:16:49.673
We've never seen them before.
I thought it'd be different.

00:16:49.881 --> 00:16:52.049
- Bright Eyes, really?
- Yes.

00:16:54.301 --> 00:16:56.510
- Summer, you got... Right there.
- Where?

00:16:57.678 --> 00:16:59.429
- Hey.
- Hey, you guys.

00:16:59.637 --> 00:17:01.597
- Hey, Summer. Hi, Danny.
- Hey. Oh, Seth.

00:17:01.805 --> 00:17:04.390
You got a little nasty there.

00:17:04.599 --> 00:17:06.016
- Okay.
- No, seriously.

00:17:06.225 --> 00:17:08.309
You got a tuna stain or something.

00:17:08.518 --> 00:17:12.145
- Well, I'll be sure and get it washed.
- Seth, seriously. All kidding aside...

00:17:12.354 --> 00:17:15.731
...you've got something there, and
I think you're gonna wanna clean it up.

00:17:18.191 --> 00:17:21.526
- Seth, you do have something there.
- What?

00:17:24.194 --> 00:17:27.822
- You got me.
- God, isn't he, like, the funniest guy ever?

00:17:28.113 --> 00:17:29.781
- Yes.
- Hey.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.782
You wanna come over later?
I TiVo-ed Leno.

00:17:31.991 --> 00:17:33.659
Sure.

00:17:36.494 --> 00:17:38.912
God. Who watches Leno?
That explains everything.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.455
- Explains what?
- Why that Danny guy is so not funny.

00:17:41.664 --> 00:17:43.540
- He's funny.
- No, he's not funny, okay?

00:17:43.748 --> 00:17:46.000
- He's big. Big is not funny.
- Whatever.

00:17:46.208 --> 00:17:50.127
- Seth. Friday night. Bright Eyes?
- Anyone can be big. That's my point.

00:17:50.336 --> 00:17:53.212
Right? Being obvious,
there's no accomplishment in that.

00:17:53.796 --> 00:17:55.714
- What?
- You're jealous.

00:17:55.922 --> 00:17:58.674
Of Danny's comedy?
No, sweetie, I'm not.

00:17:58.883 --> 00:18:02.593
No, of Danny. If you weren't,
you'd be happy for Summer.

00:18:02.802 --> 00:18:04.636
You'd embrace the friend.

00:18:13.517 --> 00:18:16.185
I love this place. All it needs
is a little nip and a tuck.

00:18:16.394 --> 00:18:18.270
But are we the right doctors for the job?

00:18:18.478 --> 00:18:21.563
Hands of a surgeon. Come on, Coop.
Get excited. Get involved.

00:18:21.772 --> 00:18:23.940
We'll blow this wall out,
make it all one room.

00:18:24.148 --> 00:18:26.442
Big leather booths.
Keep it dark, but not too dark.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.901
You know, just like it was
for Bogie and Bacall.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:32.028
- You're serious about this, aren't you?
- Yeah. What do you got?

00:18:32.695 --> 00:18:35.739
- They used to have great live music here.
- I like it. Cabaret?

00:18:35.947 --> 00:18:37.782
- Actually, jazz.
- Jazz works. That's good.

00:18:38.199 --> 00:18:39.950
- How about a raw bar?
- Okay.

00:18:40.158 --> 00:18:41.993
- As long as it feels timeless.
- It will.

00:18:42.201 --> 00:18:46.079
Gary Cooper was a big oyster man.
And a big drinker.

00:18:46.287 --> 00:18:48.289
Okay, so no frou-frou drinks.
No umbrellas.

00:18:48.497 --> 00:18:50.748
No fruit wedges.
Nothing Gary wouldn't approve of.

00:18:50.957 --> 00:18:54.793
- Only one kind of martini.
- Thank you. And only the finest Scotch.

00:18:55.084 --> 00:18:57.378
Now, we're gonna have
to have meat loaf on the menu.

00:18:57.586 --> 00:18:59.295
My mother makes
the greatest meat loaf.

00:18:59.504 --> 00:19:01.588
- I can get the recipe.
- No, my mother makes...

00:19:01.797 --> 00:19:04.173
...the greatest meat loaf,
and I have the recipe.

00:19:05.633 --> 00:19:07.342
There can be two meat loafs
on the menu.

00:19:07.551 --> 00:19:09.218
We'll make restaurant history.

00:19:09.427 --> 00:19:12.345
Hello, Lighthouse. Your ship has come in.

00:19:12.595 --> 00:19:14.972
Now, you know where you're going
for the slate, yes?

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:18.974
Brenda Antin has the seagrass mats, and
Betsie von Toff is going to do the flowers.

00:19:19.183 --> 00:19:21.476
Hydrangeas only, people. Okay.

00:19:21.684 --> 00:19:23.477
We have 72 hours
to make this open house.

00:19:23.686 --> 00:19:25.645
I want a full progress report
and POs today.

00:19:25.854 --> 00:19:27.980
Let's get it done. Go.

00:19:31.232 --> 00:19:33.942
Hey. Sorry about your office, Kiki.
I needed a base camp...

00:19:34.192 --> 00:19:36.110
...for Operation Model Home.
- Okay, Julie.

00:19:36.319 --> 00:19:40.363
I think maybe a little bit
you've lost your mind. This is a disaster.

00:19:40.571 --> 00:19:43.114
Kirsten, if you stopped open-heart
surgery halfway through...

00:19:43.323 --> 00:19:44.615
...it would look like murder.

00:19:44.824 --> 00:19:49.327
You have 72 hours.
I gave you a list of the usual vendors.

00:19:49.535 --> 00:19:51.495
See, there's that word, "usual."

00:19:51.703 --> 00:19:55.372
What I'm doing is special. It's inspired.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.416
- You're never gonna get done in time.
- Good attitude.

00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:01.543
Thanks for putting that out
in the universe.

00:20:01.751 --> 00:20:06.379
All you need is a few accent rugs,
a couch, maybe a potted plant.

00:20:06.587 --> 00:20:09.506
- We're selling a space.
- Well, I'm selling a lifestyle.

00:20:09.714 --> 00:20:13.175
Kirsten, the Newport Group
should be an aspirational brand.

00:20:13.383 --> 00:20:15.551
"Aspirational"? Is that even a word?

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.429
I know it seems ambitious.
And it'll be expensive, but sometimes...

00:20:19.637 --> 00:20:22.097
...you gotta spend money to make money.

00:20:22.764 --> 00:20:25.141
Hey, are you hungry? I'm starved.

00:21:13.921 --> 00:21:17.215
Why'd you do it? If they vote to expel
you, there's nothing we can do.

00:21:17.423 --> 00:21:21.051
You will have taken this opportunity
and tanked it. And why?

00:21:21.343 --> 00:21:24.886
- Are you jealous of this Oliver kid?
- No. No, I'm not jealous.

00:21:25.428 --> 00:21:28.180
Look, you guys may not believe me.
No one may believe me.

00:21:28.347 --> 00:21:32.224
The first time I met the kid, he was in jail.
He has a medical history. You're right.

00:21:32.433 --> 00:21:35.393
Okay. He's trouble. Now you're
the one who might be expelled.

00:21:35.601 --> 00:21:38.687
- Lf only you had come to us.
- I wanted to deal with it myself.

00:21:38.895 --> 00:21:40.605
- Well done.
- Do you know how hard we...?

00:21:40.813 --> 00:21:43.565
- You worked to get into that school?
- You can't help Marissa.

00:21:43.773 --> 00:21:47.234
- You can't even help yourself.
- Okay. I screwed up, yet again.

00:21:48.484 --> 00:21:50.236
So now what?

00:21:50.944 --> 00:21:52.153
You gonna kick me out?

00:21:54.905 --> 00:21:58.074
You think you can mess up so bad
we'll just give up on you? You can't.

00:21:58.282 --> 00:22:02.035
You are part of this family now, and
you're gonna feel the full weight of that.

00:22:02.243 --> 00:22:04.703
You're gonna wish we threw you out.

00:22:23.423 --> 00:22:24.799
Hey, man.

00:22:25.841 --> 00:22:28.926
I couldn't help but overhear.
Actually, I was eavesdropping.

00:22:29.135 --> 00:22:30.928
They're pretty pissed, huh?

00:22:31.136 --> 00:22:34.096
- Yeah, well, I deserved it.
- Yeah?

00:22:34.638 --> 00:22:38.474
Well, good. So this is over then, though?
I mean, lesson learned and all that?

00:22:45.478 --> 00:22:49.398
Today I saw Oliver give Marissa a letter...

00:22:49.606 --> 00:22:51.482
...which she put in her locker.

00:22:56.152 --> 00:23:01.280
And seeing Oliver do this inspired you
to write a letter of your own?

00:23:02.948 --> 00:23:05.241
So this is Oliver's letter.

00:23:05.991 --> 00:23:08.076
That Marissa asked you to mail?

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:11.578
- I took it from her locker.
- Dude, what is wrong with you?

00:23:11.745 --> 00:23:13.287
- You haven't read it?
- No, not yet.

00:23:13.496 --> 00:23:16.039
Not ever. You can't read it.
You have to put it back.

00:23:16.248 --> 00:23:18.457
What if he's after her? He's a sick kid.

00:23:18.666 --> 00:23:21.126
Oliver has not done anything to Marissa
except be her friend.

00:23:21.543 --> 00:23:23.794
Okay, stop it.
You're in enough trouble already.

00:23:24.044 --> 00:23:26.879
And honestly, you're starting
to freak me out a little bit.

00:23:28.797 --> 00:23:32.299
Just... Will you promise me
that you will put it back?

00:23:33.842 --> 00:23:36.510
Will you promise me
that you will put it back?

00:23:41.889 --> 00:23:43.765
- Put it back.
- I will.

00:23:43.973 --> 00:23:45.182
Put it back.

00:24:27.501 --> 00:24:29.043
Come in.

00:24:30.753 --> 00:24:32.170
Hey, man.

00:24:35.964 --> 00:24:39.258
Okay, I know everything you said
last night, but I need to talk to you.

00:24:39.466 --> 00:24:41.343
- You read it?
- It's worse than I imagined.

00:24:41.551 --> 00:24:44.094
- No, please don't.
- He says he can't live without her...

00:24:44.303 --> 00:24:46.596
I don't wanna hear it.
That letter's like The Ring.

00:24:46.804 --> 00:24:49.681
Anyone who reads it is gonna die.
Plus, it's a federal offense.

00:24:49.890 --> 00:24:52.349
- Okay. I'm being serious.
- So am I. Okay?

00:24:52.558 --> 00:24:56.143
That is Marissa's letter
that you stole from her locker and read?

00:24:56.352 --> 00:24:58.311
- Lf she finds out, you guys are done.
- Okay.

00:24:58.520 --> 00:25:00.521
- I get that. Oliver...
- Oliver might be crazy.

00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:04.107
You might be right. But right now,
you're giving him a run for his money.

00:25:04.899 --> 00:25:07.734
Hey, Seth. Is Ryan in there?

00:25:08.193 --> 00:25:09.735
Yeah. Hey.

00:25:12.654 --> 00:25:14.488
Hey. What are you guys doing?

00:25:14.697 --> 00:25:16.906
Ryan was waxing my back.
Could you give us a sec?

00:25:17.157 --> 00:25:19.616
Sure. I just wanted to know
if after school today...

00:25:19.825 --> 00:25:22.368
...you wanted to take
that cooking lesson with Oliver?

00:25:23.661 --> 00:25:28.205
I can't. I'm helping Kirsten move furniture
in the new model home.

00:25:39.962 --> 00:25:41.172
Julie?

00:25:47.759 --> 00:25:49.051
It's a disaster.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.053
What was all that
about open-heart surgery?

00:25:51.261 --> 00:25:52.554
I lost the patient.

00:25:57.015 --> 00:25:58.849
- What happened?
- It's what didn't happen.

00:25:59.350 --> 00:26:04.561
No slate. No bubbling fountains.
No seagrass.

00:26:05.604 --> 00:26:07.063
Hydrangeas are out of season.

00:26:07.355 --> 00:26:10.231
We have 48 hours until the open house,
and we have nothing.

00:26:10.440 --> 00:26:12.149
- We can fix this.
- No, we can't.

00:26:12.775 --> 00:26:14.359
Way to put that into the universe.

00:26:14.943 --> 00:26:18.361
I'll call my vendors.
It may not be anything special.

00:26:18.737 --> 00:26:20.321
It may not be "aspirational."

00:26:20.529 --> 00:26:23.740
God, I don't give a rat's ass.
If Caleb sees that house empty...

00:26:23.948 --> 00:26:27.659
He won't. But you gotta be ready
to work. Get your hands dirty.

00:26:29.118 --> 00:26:30.536
Manicure's not till Friday.

00:26:36.748 --> 00:26:39.917
Can I have an orange-peel smoothie
with a splash of pineapple, please?

00:26:40.125 --> 00:26:41.918
I'll have the same.

00:26:42.168 --> 00:26:45.420
Except with some strawberry and banana.

00:26:51.215 --> 00:26:54.592
Mr. Palmer totally looks like a pterodactyl.

00:26:54.843 --> 00:26:56.594
God, he does impersonations?

00:26:58.428 --> 00:27:01.430
Hey, why you all up in my Kool-Aid
not even knowing the flavor?

00:27:02.723 --> 00:27:04.015
- Hey, Summer.
- What?

00:27:04.223 --> 00:27:05.849
- You know who wants a smoothie?
- Who?

00:27:06.058 --> 00:27:09.435
- Mr. Chuckle!
- No! Oh, my God.

00:27:13.396 --> 00:27:15.355
Danny. Hey, what are you
doing after school?

00:27:15.564 --> 00:27:17.857
You wanna maybe come over
and hang out at my house?

00:27:18.065 --> 00:27:20.525
I've TiVo-ed some Leno.
Seann William Scott's on.

00:27:20.734 --> 00:27:24.111
Oh, Leno. Sean William Scott. Nice.
Double the comedy.

00:27:24.319 --> 00:27:25.695
Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't see it.

00:27:32.449 --> 00:27:34.159
Hey, man. I thought you were in court.

00:27:34.367 --> 00:27:37.036
No, it's a settlement.
I almost never go to court anymore.

00:27:37.202 --> 00:27:41.205
So order up some martinis and meat loaf.
We got ourselves a restaurant.

00:27:43.164 --> 00:27:45.833
Well, I thought you'd be
a little more excited.

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:47.959
- What'd you do?
- I put a down payment on it.

00:27:48.168 --> 00:27:49.627
Tomorrow we go sign the title.

00:27:49.835 --> 00:27:52.629
I haven't had a chance to come up
with my share of the money.

00:27:52.837 --> 00:27:55.964
No, I covered it. We can work out
a get-even scheme once we're afloat.

00:27:56.173 --> 00:27:59.300
- So, what? I work for you?
- Jimmy, come on.

00:27:59.508 --> 00:28:01.926
You were one click away
from manning the mechanical bull...

00:28:02.135 --> 00:28:03.177
...at the new cowboy bar.

00:28:03.385 --> 00:28:06.637
I wanna pull my own weight. You've
already done enough for me as it is.

00:28:06.846 --> 00:28:08.305
I'm not doing it just for you.

00:28:08.514 --> 00:28:11.932
This could mean freedom for both of us.
You could stay at a job you like...

00:28:12.141 --> 00:28:15.893
...and it'd give me a break from all
my rich clients and the office politics.

00:28:16.102 --> 00:28:18.645
- We could work for ourselves.
- I don't know, Sandy.

00:28:18.853 --> 00:28:21.730
- I think I need more time to...
- How much more time do you need?

00:28:21.980 --> 00:28:23.606
It's too fast. It's too soon.

00:28:23.857 --> 00:28:27.067
Okay. Great. Great. I got an idea.
Let's wait till we're dead.

00:28:27.859 --> 00:28:29.652
I gotta go settle.

00:28:52.499 --> 00:28:55.793
That is so cool
that you know Marissa's combo.

00:28:56.002 --> 00:28:57.378
Shows a lot of trust.

00:28:58.378 --> 00:28:59.921
- Yeah, for emergencies.
- Oh, yeah?

00:29:00.129 --> 00:29:05.174
What's the emergency? Ran out
of erasers? No more ink left in your pen?

00:29:05.383 --> 00:29:07.967
No, it's a book I forgot.

00:29:08.426 --> 00:29:09.677
Just kidding around, man.

00:29:12.470 --> 00:29:14.847
Last class of the day
is so tough to get through.

00:29:15.055 --> 00:29:16.806
- Feel you on that one.
- What's up?

00:29:17.223 --> 00:29:19.892
Hey, Marissa and I were
talking about a camping trip.

00:29:20.058 --> 00:29:22.268
Santa Monica mountains?
Bring the whole gang?

00:29:23.227 --> 00:29:24.770
- Sure. Yeah.
- Sounds awesome, man.

00:29:24.978 --> 00:29:27.188
All right. I'll let her know that you are in.

00:29:28.772 --> 00:29:32.858
Long bathroom break.
I should go. See you.

00:29:37.694 --> 00:29:39.362
I do not like that kid at all.

00:29:39.904 --> 00:29:41.614
Yeah? Don't you think that...?

00:29:41.905 --> 00:29:44.282
He's here for Marissa. Hell, yeah.

00:29:44.907 --> 00:29:47.659
You gotta let that guy know, "back off."

00:29:48.034 --> 00:29:49.452
I'll do it for you, if you want.

00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:52.537
- I'll keep that in mind.
- Just give me the word...

00:29:52.745 --> 00:29:55.581
...and I will drop the Great Gatsby.

00:30:02.085 --> 00:30:04.961
Did your mama teach you
how to play this game?

00:30:05.170 --> 00:30:07.463
You didn't think I'd pack the heat,
did you?

00:30:07.671 --> 00:30:11.049
Think you can just get me here, huh?
Home court advantage. Guess what.

00:30:11.257 --> 00:30:14.009
Who's got the secret codes? Danny does.

00:30:14.676 --> 00:30:17.803
Guess what, buddy. You are Punk'd.

00:30:18.011 --> 00:30:20.888
There's a camera there, camera there
and a camera right there.

00:30:21.097 --> 00:30:22.264
- Who's your daddy?
- Hey, kid.

00:30:22.472 --> 00:30:25.057
Settlement happened sooner
than I thought.

00:30:25.266 --> 00:30:28.685
- Good. This is my friend Danny.
- Hey. How are you? I'm Sandy.

00:30:29.102 --> 00:30:30.602
Why don't you take a shower?

00:30:31.770 --> 00:30:35.397
- Pardon me?
- Just kidding. I like you dirty.

00:30:36.314 --> 00:30:39.316
Sandy. Dirty. Sandy. Dirty.

00:30:41.568 --> 00:30:44.903
- That kid is not funny.
- Thank you. I know.

00:30:45.153 --> 00:30:48.822
- He makes Ryan look funny.
- He makes Marissa look funny.

00:30:49.031 --> 00:30:54.743
Gentiles. I love your mother
more than words, but not funny.

00:30:54.951 --> 00:30:57.411
Get yourself some funnier friends.

00:31:02.622 --> 00:31:04.082
- There you are.
- Thanks, man.

00:31:04.290 --> 00:31:07.542
- Sure.
- I'm so parched.

00:31:10.711 --> 00:31:14.088
Oh, dude. Have you seen
my impression of Mr. Parker?

00:31:14.296 --> 00:31:16.506
Yes. Pterodactyl. Seen it. It's good.

00:31:19.425 --> 00:31:22.552
- Hey, listen, man. Can I ask you a favor?
- Sure.

00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:25.428
Whenever you're around Summer,
could you...?

00:31:25.595 --> 00:31:29.389
This is weird, but could you try
and be a little less funny?

00:31:29.598 --> 00:31:32.600
Man, all I ever hear from her
is how funny Seth Cohen is.

00:31:32.808 --> 00:31:35.476
How he's the funniest guy
she's ever met.

00:31:35.643 --> 00:31:39.979
I mean, I like her so much, and I'm just...
I'm killing myself to hang in there.

00:31:41.897 --> 00:31:45.441
She said that about me,
that she thinks I'm the funniest guy ever?

00:31:45.649 --> 00:31:48.693
Yes. You and some dude
named Captain Oats.

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:52.695
Who the hell is Captain Oats?

00:31:53.446 --> 00:31:56.281
Well, chin up, Danny.
Because you know what?

00:31:56.656 --> 00:32:00.784
I think you're funny. I just think,
and if you don't mind me saying so...

00:32:00.992 --> 00:32:05.203
...that you could go a little bigger
with your comedy. I think you're small...

00:32:05.370 --> 00:32:07.163
...a little under the radar.
- Yeah?

00:32:07.371 --> 00:32:09.206
- Yeah, big's hilarious.
- Big.

00:32:09.414 --> 00:32:11.249
- Yeah.
- All right, man. Thanks.

00:32:11.457 --> 00:32:13.208
- I'll give that a shot.
- Give it a shot.

00:32:13.417 --> 00:32:15.126
I'll give it a shot!

00:32:15.418 --> 00:32:17.961
Thanks for making time for me
after school.

00:32:18.170 --> 00:32:22.089
- I know how busy you are.
- Of course. What's going on?

00:32:22.339 --> 00:32:24.424
Why don't you have a seat.

00:32:28.259 --> 00:32:33.388
So I know this is a little outside
my job description as dean.

00:32:33.679 --> 00:32:37.974
I felt I had a responsibility
to have an honest conversation with you.

00:32:38.474 --> 00:32:40.434
- What is it?
- I need to talk to you about...

00:32:40.642 --> 00:32:43.977
...one of our transfer students, with
whom I know you have a relationship.

00:32:44.186 --> 00:32:48.480
- And who I worry might not be so stable.
- I appreciate it, Dr. Kim.

00:32:48.689 --> 00:32:51.107
But I'm well aware of Oliver's issues.

00:32:51.315 --> 00:32:53.483
It's not Oliver I want to talk about.

00:33:13.037 --> 00:33:16.248
Detention's over, gentlemen.
See you tomorrow.

00:33:28.881 --> 00:33:30.882
I thought you were helping Kirsten.

00:33:31.632 --> 00:33:36.010
- I got detention.
- I see that. What for?

00:33:37.428 --> 00:33:40.263
I failed this chemistry quiz,
slacking off on some homework.

00:33:40.721 --> 00:33:41.930
That's a lie.

00:33:43.765 --> 00:33:48.101
- What are you talking about?
- I heard what happened, your break-in.

00:33:50.186 --> 00:33:53.813
- I did it to protect you.
- What? What are you talking about?

00:33:54.021 --> 00:33:56.940
I don't trust him. He has a history
of girls he's obsessed with.

00:33:57.148 --> 00:33:58.482
He's not obsessed with me.

00:33:59.066 --> 00:34:01.818
You know, ever since he showed up,
you never trusted him.

00:34:02.026 --> 00:34:04.194
And okay, that's who you are...

00:34:04.403 --> 00:34:07.071
...but you have to trust me.
- The kid has serious issues.

00:34:07.238 --> 00:34:09.739
- Who doesn't?
- He's in love with you.

00:34:10.073 --> 00:34:11.365
We're just friends.

00:34:13.325 --> 00:34:14.534
Yeah.

00:34:16.577 --> 00:34:18.495
Then what's this?

00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:22.539
Where did you get this?

00:34:25.875 --> 00:34:27.626
You stole it from my locker?

00:34:29.835 --> 00:34:31.711
I've been looking everywhere for this.

00:34:32.212 --> 00:34:33.754
So you know what this is?
What this says?

00:34:33.921 --> 00:34:35.130
I can't believe you.

00:34:35.380 --> 00:34:37.799
I can't believe you stole it. You read it.

00:34:38.007 --> 00:34:40.050
How can you say
he's not in love with you?

00:34:40.258 --> 00:34:43.552
Because he didn't write it to me.
He wrote it to Natalie.

00:34:43.761 --> 00:34:48.055
He wants to get back together with her.
And he just wanted me to read it first.

00:34:54.100 --> 00:34:57.102
- Look, I'm sorry.
- I can't do this anymore.

00:35:02.105 --> 00:35:03.857
Because now...

00:35:04.607 --> 00:35:06.775
...I don't trust you.

00:35:22.618 --> 00:35:25.203
- Morning.
- Morning.

00:35:26.120 --> 00:35:27.413
You okay?

00:35:27.621 --> 00:35:30.498
Well, I'm supposed to sign
the title on the Lighthouse today.

00:35:30.707 --> 00:35:32.583
I can't believe
you're buying a restaurant.

00:35:32.791 --> 00:35:35.918
Funny. That's what Jimmy said
just before he backed out.

00:35:36.127 --> 00:35:37.711
He did?

00:35:38.462 --> 00:35:42.964
I know the whole idea seems crazy,
but I thought that was part of the appeal.

00:35:43.298 --> 00:35:47.009
- Well, what are you gonna do?
- I'm gonna have to buy a little time...

00:35:47.217 --> 00:35:48.426
...and not lose the place.

00:35:48.635 --> 00:35:52.595
Well, you can always hire Julie
as a partner. I think she'll be available.

00:35:52.804 --> 00:35:55.347
I have to show my father
the model home this morning...

00:35:55.556 --> 00:35:57.849
...and we had no time to pull it together.

00:35:58.057 --> 00:36:01.518
- I believe he will be underwhelmed.
- The Coopers keep things unpredictable.

00:36:01.726 --> 00:36:03.936
No. I predicted that Julie would be fired.

00:36:04.144 --> 00:36:06.020
Top of the morning to you, son.

00:36:06.521 --> 00:36:09.898
- You talk to Ryan last night?
- No, he just came home and went to bed.

00:36:11.899 --> 00:36:16.110
Hey. Do you want something to eat?
You missed dinner, you must be hungry.

00:36:16.319 --> 00:36:18.820
- I'm okay. Thanks.
- What time's Marissa picking you up?

00:36:19.029 --> 00:36:22.239
- I was gonna maybe go early with Anna.
- Marissa's not picking me up.

00:36:33.621 --> 00:36:35.289
He hasn't called yet.

00:36:35.914 --> 00:36:38.374
- I know.
- Is it bad that he hasn't called yet?

00:36:38.582 --> 00:36:40.709
It doesn't mean anything.

00:36:41.418 --> 00:36:43.252
Here you go, Mr. Nichol.

00:36:45.295 --> 00:36:46.504
- Hello.
- Hi, Cal.

00:36:46.713 --> 00:36:48.047
Hey, Dad.

00:36:48.255 --> 00:36:50.090
I just got back
from the new development.

00:36:50.340 --> 00:36:54.551
Look, it was short notice and
Julie did the best she could, considering.

00:36:55.426 --> 00:36:58.386
You're preaching to the converted.
I loved it.

00:36:58.595 --> 00:37:00.805
The d Ácor was simple, classic.
The way I like it.

00:37:01.263 --> 00:37:03.932
It allows the architecture and views
to sell themselves.

00:37:04.182 --> 00:37:05.433
- You're happy?
- You're happy?

00:37:05.641 --> 00:37:09.769
Pleased as punch. How Julie here
hit one out of the park on her first swing.

00:37:12.437 --> 00:37:15.105
What can I say? It's my true passion.

00:37:15.814 --> 00:37:17.565
Well, now your passion's your job.

00:37:17.774 --> 00:37:20.692
Kiki, stop looking for a new decorator.
We've found our girl.

00:37:20.901 --> 00:37:22.068
- We have?
- We have?

00:37:22.276 --> 00:37:25.403
The fact that you two are such close
friends makes the decision easier.

00:37:25.612 --> 00:37:29.072
Be fun. You two working together,
side by side.

00:37:32.575 --> 00:37:36.327
Have you lost your mind, Kiki?
That thing is unsightly.

00:37:38.578 --> 00:37:41.122
Well, who could have predicted this?

00:37:42.789 --> 00:37:45.791
- Hey, Summer.
- Hey, Cohen.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.209
How are you?

00:37:47.417 --> 00:37:49.543
- Okay.
- Yeah?

00:37:50.252 --> 00:37:54.046
It's just Danny.
I mean, he was, like, really funny, right?

00:37:54.713 --> 00:37:57.757
- Yeah.
- And now, all of a sudden, he's gotten...

00:37:58.632 --> 00:37:59.883
...big.

00:38:00.092 --> 00:38:03.094
Hey, Seth. Check it out!

00:38:03.594 --> 00:38:05.512
Get off me!

00:38:07.096 --> 00:38:10.223
- Now, that's funny.
- Yeah.

00:38:10.557 --> 00:38:12.016
Well, that's the end of him.

00:38:12.474 --> 00:38:16.560
I guess I really will end up
bitter and alone.

00:38:18.103 --> 00:38:19.646
Hey.

00:38:19.854 --> 00:38:21.730
I'm sorry.

00:38:22.522 --> 00:38:24.649
And I thought he was a good one.

00:38:25.983 --> 00:38:29.110
But I guess people can be
really unpredictable.

00:38:29.652 --> 00:38:30.944
You know?

00:38:32.904 --> 00:38:36.114
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:38:36.323 --> 00:38:38.366
- Nice scarf.
- You too.

00:38:39.283 --> 00:38:42.201
- So it's croque-monsieur Thursday.
- Yes, it is.

00:38:42.410 --> 00:38:45.620
- I was thinking fish sticks.
- I was gonna have peanut butter and jelly.

00:38:45.829 --> 00:38:49.456
That's great.
Well, I'm gonna just go wash up.

00:38:49.664 --> 00:38:50.873
- We'll go eat?
- Okay.

00:38:51.082 --> 00:38:53.625
All right. Bye.

00:38:59.212 --> 00:39:02.381
- Well, I'm gonna go.
- Yeah, well.

00:39:02.673 --> 00:39:05.466
I have to go ice Big Funny Guy, so...

00:39:06.008 --> 00:39:07.842
Well, if you're ever feeling, you know...

00:39:08.093 --> 00:39:10.844
...too bitter and Ionely,
I TiVo-ed some Daily Shows.

00:39:11.053 --> 00:39:13.721
I know Jon Stewart's no Leno.

00:39:15.847 --> 00:39:17.265
Thanks.

00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:05.337
My dad died and left me this place.
I never thought I'd have to sell it.

00:40:05.545 --> 00:40:08.547
It was such a magical spot,
when I was a kid.

00:40:08.755 --> 00:40:11.340
Don't sell it. Just give me
more time to find a partner.

00:40:11.549 --> 00:40:14.843
Sandy, I got two other offers
on the table. I can't wait any longer.

00:40:15.051 --> 00:40:16.594
I understand.

00:40:17.219 --> 00:40:19.054
I'm not too late, am I?

00:40:19.262 --> 00:40:20.930
Who's this?

00:40:21.138 --> 00:40:22.973
My partner.

00:40:23.890 --> 00:40:25.349
I found him.

00:40:25.558 --> 00:40:29.310
That conversation we just had about not
wanting to buy the place? Forget it.

00:40:30.894 --> 00:40:33.938
Look, you know, this could fail.
I mean, you know...

00:40:34.146 --> 00:40:37.357
...I could fail again. I pretty much
only have a legacy of failure.

00:40:37.565 --> 00:40:40.734
I could be responsible for ruining
this place, ruining our friendship.

00:40:40.942 --> 00:40:42.652
Jimmy. Just sign it.

00:40:52.158 --> 00:40:53.617
Okay.

00:41:02.497 --> 00:41:04.874
I heard what happened
between you and Marissa.

00:41:07.209 --> 00:41:08.668
Yeah.

00:41:10.794 --> 00:41:12.462
I'm sorry.

00:41:12.670 --> 00:41:15.255
- It's okay.
- No, it's not.

00:41:15.881 --> 00:41:17.799
I was wrong about you.

00:41:19.425 --> 00:41:24.219
Well, I mean, did you think I came here
because of Marissa?

00:41:24.845 --> 00:41:27.430
What, because I'm in love with her?

00:41:27.638 --> 00:41:29.556
Yeah. No. I...

00:41:31.099 --> 00:41:32.683
It was crazy.

00:41:38.937 --> 00:41:42.814
Here's the deal, Ryan.
And it's nothing personal.

00:41:44.107 --> 00:41:47.067
But Marissa and I, we just connect.

00:41:48.193 --> 00:41:51.445
She understands me, gets me.

00:41:51.653 --> 00:41:54.113
I don't know if there's only one person
on the planet...

00:41:54.321 --> 00:41:55.781
...you're supposed to be with...

00:41:55.989 --> 00:41:59.575
...but when she and I are together,
sure feels that way.

00:42:01.284 --> 00:42:04.578
I'm sorry, but you and Marissa?
Come on, man.

00:42:04.786 --> 00:42:07.288
- You're from different worlds.
- You stay away from her.

00:42:07.496 --> 00:42:09.956
You can't fight fate, man.

00:42:11.165 --> 00:42:14.542
I didn't even have to lift a finger,
and look what happened to you guys.

00:42:14.751 --> 00:42:17.628
Because you're not supposed
to be together.

00:42:17.878 --> 00:42:20.213
I'm not saying
you didn't serve your purpose.

00:42:20.421 --> 00:42:23.381
If it wasn't for you,
she would've never gone to therapy.

00:42:23.673 --> 00:42:27.300
- She never would've met me.
- I am not gonna let this happen.

00:42:27.509 --> 00:42:30.427
At this point, who's gonna believe you?

00:42:31.428 --> 00:42:32.762
Walk away...

00:42:32.971 --> 00:42:35.264
...you have a chance
to make something of yourself.

00:42:35.514 --> 00:42:39.266
Don't blow it over some chick
you're not gonna care about in 10 years.

00:42:39.933 --> 00:42:41.142
Okay?

00:42:42.268 --> 00:42:43.686
I really am sorry.

00:42:53.859 --> 00:42:55.943
Hey! Hey! Back off!

00:42:56.944 --> 00:42:58.695
Get off me!

00:42:59.154 --> 00:43:00.363
Get off me!

00:43:01.155 --> 00:43:03.365
Stay away from her! Stay away from her!
